From 874ced7e09987793d01b84b4be4a8f4ec9f51454 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 19:19:19 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] feat(drilling): ream cycle (G85) as a drill operation
 parameter

Ream is a new cycle choice and CL cycle kind: feed in, feed back out at
the same feed, no dwell (RS-274/NGC G85, NIST IR 6556). Canned-cycle
posts write G85 and refuse an unknown cycle word by name instead of
posting it as another cycle; Heidenhain, TinyG and Carvera post the
expanded feed-out chain; posts without drilling refuse it. The ream
rides the bore door (tool must fit, stepped hole refused, pre-drilled)
and is never chosen by Auto. Command, project file, MCP edit_operation
and the drill page's Cycle combo carry it; programs that do not choose
it post byte-identical.

Refs #1445

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
